<title>BELGIUM: No reason Germany will fail EMU tests - Zalm.</title>
<headline>No reason Germany will fail EMU tests - Zalm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm said on Monday there was no reason to expect that Germany would fail to meet the preconditions of a single EU currency.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no reason to think (Germany) will not meet the criteria,&quot; Zalm told a news conference after a meeting of EU finance ministers.</p>
<p>While he acknowledged that recent German employment figures were disappointing, a stronger dollar and lower long-term interest rates were positive developments for Germany. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
